Description: Structural Memory Protocol - Graph-based Codebase Intelligence for AI Agents
 SMP (Structural Memory Protocol) is a graph-based codebase intelligence system
 for AI agents. It parses source code (14 languages via tree-sitter) into a
 knowledge graph stored in a memory-mapped journal, exposing a JSON-RPC API
 via FastAPI and an MCP server over stdio for agents.
 .
 Features:
  * Multi-language code parsing (Python, JavaScript, TypeScript, Java, C/C++,
    C#, Go, Rust, PHP, Ruby, Swift, Kotlin, MATLAB)
  * Graph-based code navigation and impact analysis
  * Semantic search using Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B GGUF model (1024 dimensions)
  * JSON-RPC API and MCP server for AI agent integration
  * Session management with safety features (locks, checkpoints, rollback)
  * Code review and PR handoff workflows
  * Community detection for architecture analysis
  * Graph integrity verification and backup/restore